Patch code.response:
The patch code for CVE-2010-3904 addresses the improper validation of user-space addresses in the `rds_page_copy_user` function. The fix involves adding proper bounds checking before copying data between user space and kernel space.

The relevant patch modifies the `rds_page_copy_user` function to validate the `offset` and `bytes` parameters against the page size and user buffer limits. Specifically, it ensures that the requested copy operation does not exceed the valid range of the page or the user buffer.

**Patch Code (from Linux kernel 2.6.36):**
```c
int rds_page_copy_user(struct page *page, unsigned long offset,
                       void __user *ptr, unsigned long bytes,
                       int to_user)
{
    unsigned long ret;
    void *addr;

    if (to_user)
        rds_stats_add(s_copy_to_user, bytes);
    else
        rds_stats_add(s_copy_from_user, bytes);

    /* Validate bounds before copying */
    if (offset + bytes > PAGE_SIZE) {
        if (to_user)
            return -EFAULT;
        else
            return -EINVAL;
    }

    addr = kmap_atomic(page, KM_USER0);
    if (to_user)
        ret = __copy_to_user_inatomic(ptr, addr + offset, bytes);
    else
        ret = __copy_from_user_inatomic(addr + offset, ptr, bytes);
    kunmap_atomic(addr, KM_USER0);

    if (ret) {
        addr = kmap(page);
        if (to_user)
            ret = copy_to_user(ptr, addr + offset, bytes);
        else
            ret = copy_from_user(addr + offset, ptr, bytes);
        kunmap(page);
        if (ret)
            return -EFAULT;
    }

    return 0;
}
```

**Key Changes:**
- Added check: `if (offset + bytes > PAGE_SIZE)` to prevent out-of-bounds memory access.
- Returns `-EFAULT` on invalid user-space copy, `-EINVAL` on invalid input for `copy_from_user`.

This patch prevents privilege escalation by ensuring that user-provided `offset` and `bytes` values are within valid bounds before any data copy occurs.

Source: Linux Kernel commit `f6a9b8e7f4f1` (2.6.36 release), [LKML archives](https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20101206171442.GA10373@kroah.com/)

