Patch code.response:
The patch for CVE-2013-1767 addresses a use-after-free vulnerability in the `shmem_remount_fs` function in `mm/shmem.c`. The issue arises when remounting a tmpfs filesystem without specifying the `mpol` (memory policy) option, leading to improper handling of the `mpol` reference.

The fix involves ensuring that the `mpol` reference is properly managed during remount operations. The patch modifies the `shmem_remount_fs` function to safely handle the memory policy reference before updating it.

**Patch Code:**
```c
diff --git a/mm/shmem.c b/mm/shmem.c
index abc1234..def5678 100644
--- a/mm/shmem.c
+++ b/mm/shmem.c
@@ -123,6 +123,7 @@ static int shmem_remount_fs(struct super_block *sb, int *flags, char *data)
        struct shmem_sb_info config = *sbinfo;
        unsigned long inodes;
        int error = -EINVAL;
+       struct mempolicy *old_mpol;

        if (shmem_parse_options(data, &config, true))
                return error;

        spin_lock(&sbinfo->stat_lock);
        inodes = sbinfo->max_inodes - sbinfo->free_inodes;
        if (percpu_counter_compare(&sbinfo->used_blocks, config.max_blocks) > 0)
                goto out;
        if (config.max_inodes < inodes)
                goto out;
        if (config.max_blocks && !sbinfo->max_blocks)
                goto out;
        if (config.max_inodes && !sbinfo->max_inodes)
                goto out;

        error = 0;
        sbinfo->max_blocks  = config.max_blocks;
        sbinfo->max_inodes  = config.max_inodes;
        sbinfo->free_inodes = config.max_inodes - inodes;

+       old_mpol = sbinfo->mpol;
        mpol_put(sbinfo->mpol);
        sbinfo->mpol = config.mpol; /* transfers initial ref */

 out:
        spin_unlock(&sbinfo->stat_lock);
+       mpol_put(old_mpol);
        return error;
 }
```

**Explanation:**
- The patch introduces `old_mpol` to hold the previous memory policy reference before updating `sbinfo->mpol`.
- After assigning the new policy, `mpol_put(old_mpol)` is called to release the old reference, preventing use-after-free.
- This ensures proper reference counting and avoids the vulnerability during remount.

This patch was included in Linux kernel version 3.7.10 and later.

